// The workspace builds the chi and Echo adapters, the command, and the
// database tests against the core in this folder. Their go.mod files have no
// replace directives, since go install refuses a module with one, so the
// go command reads this file instead (it is never in a module that anyone
// requires). The replace covers the version the nested modules require,
// which is not on the proxy until it is tagged; scripts/release.mjs moves it
// with them. go mod tidy ignores workspaces: run node scripts/go-tidy.mjs.
go 1.25.0

use (
	.
	./chi
	./cmd/runlight
	./dbtest
	./echo
)

replace runlight.sh/go v0.0.0 => ./
